{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.LiftingDescent.HabiroCollapse","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.HabiroCollapse","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.residue_unit_gives_no_obstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.residue_unit_gives_no_obstruction","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HabiroCollapse.lean#L127-L131","doc":"The shape of the gap, stated so it cannot be mistaken for a search that\nfailed: whenever the residue is a unit downstream, the image says nothing\nabout `x`, because `not_isUnit_of_image` runs the other way. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.isUnit_four_zmod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.isUnit_four_zmod","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HabiroCollapse.lean#L111-L125","doc":"`4` is a unit of `𝔽_p` for every odd prime — so a residue of `4` is\n**not** an obstruction, and `not_isUnit_of_image` cannot be applied to it.\n\n`O/𝔭 ≅ 𝔽_p` is where the collapse of the QOU Frobenius lands, which is why\nthis blocks the intended argument at every prime except `2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.map_habiro_expansion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.map_habiro_expansion","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HabiroCollapse.lean#L89-L109","doc":"**Habiro collapse.** Under any ring map sending `q ↦ -1`, a Habiro\nexpansion collapses to its two lowest coefficients:\n`φ (Σ_{m<N} a m · (q;q)_m) = φ (a 0) + 2 · φ (a 1)`.\n\nThis is the whole content of `h_collapse` in\n`MotivicPerpetualObstructionFromTrace.lean`, minus the single arithmetic\ninput `φ q = -1`. The `2` is `φ ((q;q)_1) = 1 - (-1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.map_qPoch_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.map_qPoch_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HabiroCollapse.lean#L76-L87","doc":"**The collapse, factor by factor.** A ring map sending `q ↦ -1` kills\n`(q;q)_m` for every `m ≥ 2`. No cyclotomic input is used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.map_qPoch_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.map_qPoch_two","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HabiroCollapse.lean#L68-L74","doc":"At `q ↦ -1` the second factor already vanishes: `1 - (-1)² = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.qPoch_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.qPoch_two","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HabiroCollapse.lean#L65-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.qPoch_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.qPoch_one","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HabiroCollapse.lean#L62-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.qPoch_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.qPoch_succ","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HabiroCollapse.lean#L59-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.qPoch_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.qPoch_zero","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HabiroCollapse.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.qPoch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.qPoch","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/HabiroCollapse.lean#L49-L55","doc":"The Habiro `q`-Pochhammer symbol `(q;q)_m = ∏_{i=1}^{m} (1 - qⁱ)`.\n\nDistinct from `QOU.MathlibExt.QuantumDilogarithm.qPochProd`, which is the\nFaddeev symbol `(-qx; q²)_N`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}